Phase 2 (FullSpectrum engine emission, P2K): collect_extruders routes
infill through the LayerTools FS-aware methods + populates
object_layer_count + treats 100%-density solid infill as sparse.

Ported from FS v0.9.9 (`ratdoux/OrcaSlicer-FullSpectrum@v0.9.9` commit
b3c41fda), `src/libslic3r/GCode/ToolOrdering.cpp` `collect_extruders`
mid-function changes.

Three changes:

1. **Populate `layer_tools.object_layer_count`** from
   `object.layers().size()` so the boundary-layer infill reversion
   gate added in patch 0036 (`use_base_infill_filament`) has the
   total layer count it needs. Without this, `object_layer_count`
   stays at the default 0 and the last-N-layers gate never fires.

2. **Rename `has_infill` to `has_sparse_infill`** and route
   `erSolidInfill` at 100% sparse density into the sparse-infill
   path. Reason: 100% density solid infill behaves identically to
   regular infill at the same density (same nozzle, same flow), so
   it should use the sparse_infill_filament selection logic. The
   prior code routed it to solid_infill_filament which can pick a
   different physical filament when an infill-filament-override is
   active.

3. **Switch the override `emplace_back` calls** from
   `resolve_filament_for_layer(region.config().X_filament, ...)` to
   `layer_tools.X_filament(region) + 1`. The methods now go through
   the FS-aware resolution chain (patches 0019 resolver + 0036
   boundary-layer + grouped manual_pattern), so the
   `layer_tools.extruders` list reflects the same physical extruder
   the per-emission code will pick.

Verified compile-clean via incremental libslic3r rebuild (3/3
objects, 0 FAILED) + ./gradlew :app:assembleDebug.

Hard dependencies:
  - patch 0028 (LayerTools::object_layer_count member declared)
  - patch 0036 (LayerTools::sparse_infill_filament + solid_infill_filament
    FS-aware bodies)
  - patch 0038 (FS region keys registered in PrintConfigDef)

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
